1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:05,666
The live dashboard is the supervisor's real-time view of the contact center.

2
00:00:05,666 --> 00:00:09,593
This video shows how to read it, how to filter the agent board,

3
00:00:09,593 --> 00:00:12,780
and what a supervisor can do from an agent's card.

4
00:00:17,380 --> 00:00:21,494
A queue that is backing up, an agent stuck on one long call,

5
00:00:21,494 --> 00:00:23,801
a service level about to break.

6
00:00:23,801 --> 00:00:28,040
A supervisor needs to see these now, not in tomorrow's report.

7
00:00:28,790 --> 00:00:33,872
The live dashboard shows how many people are waiting, which agents are free,

8
00:00:33,872 --> 00:00:35,545
and who is on a call.

9
00:00:35,545 --> 00:00:40,131
From an agent's card, a supervisor can step into the call, coach the

10
00:00:40,131 --> 00:00:42,300
agent, or take the call over.

11
00:00:46,500 --> 00:00:51,436
The dashboard shows the queues and campaigns on your own agent entitlement record,

12
00:00:51,436 --> 00:00:54,970
and you can only act on agents and calls in those queues.

13
00:00:55,720 --> 00:01:02,626
A supervisor without an entitlement record sees an empty dashboard, even with the Administrator role.

14
00:01:02,626 --> 00:01:06,950
Give each supervisor a record with the queues they supervise.

15
00:01:11,181 --> 00:01:14,307
Open Interaction Center, Live dashboard.

16
00:01:14,307 --> 00:01:18,860
The status at the top says Connected while live updates work.

17
00:01:18,860 --> 00:01:22,461
The page refreshes by itself every ten seconds.

18
00:01:22,992 --> 00:01:28,122
The summary shows the total waiting across your queues, the available agents, the

19
00:01:28,122 --> 00:01:29,832
agents, and the queues.

20
00:01:30,387 --> 00:01:32,274
Each queue has a tile:

21
00:01:32,274 --> 00:01:40,088
waiting, signed-in agents, available, busy and not-ready agents, the longest wait, and service level breaches.

22
00:01:40,088 --> 00:01:45,275
A tile turns amber when the longest wait passes half the threshold, and

23
00:01:45,275 --> 00:01:46,757
red on a breach.

24
00:01:47,261 --> 00:01:51,892
When the dialer is on, a banner above the summary says what it is doing.

25
00:01:51,892 --> 00:01:56,700
The Why isn't this dialing panel explains why work is not being dispatched.

26
00:01:56,700 --> 00:01:58,541
Here, no work is waiting.

27
00:02:02,796 --> 00:02:07,317
The agent board has one card per agent, with presence, a status badge,

28
00:02:07,317 --> 00:02:11,600
the active interactions, and the queues the agent is signed in to.

29
00:02:11,600 --> 00:02:14,456
Here the one agent is Available, and idle.

30
00:02:14,943 --> 00:02:19,665
Filter by Agent name, by Signed-in queue, and by Status:

31
00:02:19,665 --> 00:02:23,853
Available, Busy, On a call, Not ready or Offline.

32
00:02:23,853 --> 00:02:26,519
Busy groups everyone at work:

33
00:02:26,519 --> 00:02:29,413
Reserved, On a call and Wrap-up.

34
00:02:29,868 --> 00:02:32,468
The header counts the agents that match.

35
00:02:32,468 --> 00:02:35,578
The browser remembers your filters for next time.

36
00:02:39,778 --> 00:02:43,463
These actions need an agent on a call, and a real call cannot

37
00:02:43,463 --> 00:02:46,598
be placed on this site, so they are described here.

38
00:02:46,598 --> 00:02:50,888
You hear the call on your own soft phone, so keep it open and signed in.

39
00:02:51,638 --> 00:02:55,068
On the card of an agent who is on a call, Listen lets

40
00:02:55,068 --> 00:02:57,800
you hear the call while nobody hears you.

41
00:02:57,800 --> 00:03:01,173
Whisper lets only the agent hear you, to coach them.

42
00:03:01,173 --> 00:03:04,138
Barge joins the call, and everyone hears you.

43
00:03:04,888 --> 00:03:09,224
Click another mode to change how you are heard, and Stop when you are done.

44
00:03:09,224 --> 00:03:11,258
Only your part of the call ends.

45
00:03:11,258 --> 00:03:15,808
An agent who has paused the recording to take card details cannot be monitored.

46
00:03:20,008 --> 00:03:24,300
Take over hands the call to you and releases the agent, for example

47
00:03:24,300 --> 00:03:26,711
when a customer asks for a manager.

48
00:03:26,711 --> 00:03:30,828
You need an agent profile of your own, and your soft phone open.

49
00:03:31,578 --> 00:03:36,311
The more actions menu on an agent's card offers End call, Transfer, and

50
00:03:36,311 --> 00:03:40,492
Start recording or Stop recording, under your company's rules.

51
00:03:40,492 --> 00:03:44,918
A transfer goes to a queue, an available agent, or a phone number.

52
00:03:45,668 --> 00:03:49,685
The same menu can Set Available, Set Not ready or Set Break for

53
00:03:49,685 --> 00:03:53,935
an agent, Sign out of queues, and send a short Message that appears

54
00:03:53,935 --> 00:03:55,798
on the agent's soft phone.

55
00:03:59,998 --> 00:04:05,654
Monitor the Contact Center in real time lets you watch, listen, whisper, barge

56
00:04:05,654 --> 00:04:07,338
and send a message.

57
00:04:08,088 --> 00:04:13,504
Take over, end, transfer and record live Contact Center calls, and set agents'

58
00:04:13,504 --> 00:04:15,955
state, covers the other actions.

59
00:04:15,955 --> 00:04:18,212
The Supervisor role has both.

60
00:04:18,212 --> 00:04:22,468
Every action is recorded in the audit trail under your name.

61
00:04:26,668 --> 00:04:30,798
A wallboard on the floor, showing waiting counts and breaches.

62
00:04:31,548 --> 00:04:37,258
A supervisor who sees a queue backing up, and asks agents to return from a break.

63
00:04:38,008 --> 00:04:42,108
Coaching a new agent on a hard call, by whispering.

64
00:04:42,858 --> 00:04:46,388
Taking over a call when a customer asks for a manager.

65
00:04:48,388 --> 00:04:52,673
Watch the tiles, filter the board, and step in when it matters.

66
00:04:52,673 --> 00:04:54,288
Thanks for watching.

